{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions","id":998174,"title":"Abyss reactions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T04:36:30-07:00","id":998174,"title":"Abyss reactions","content":"I'm interesting how you see Abyss/Beast interaction and reactions. You know like those found in the invaders from the abyss. You can also post short snippets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:25:10-07:00","id":998199,"title":"","content":"Depends on the intrusion. Most would probably be the kind of thing that causes Begotten to awkwardly point out that just because something may or may not be family doesn't mean you have <i>only </i>a duty to help it. Sometimes you're the only creature that can stop your cousin (assuming they count as such-they're even more alien to Earth than the God-Machine, because at least the Machine can be considered a naturalized citizen of Terra at this point, gulmoth and acamoth are more akin to reality's barbarians at the gates that occasionally sneak in to ruin everyone's days). Sometimes the Beast may not realize the spatial anomaly is actually a creature in its own right (see the Twisting Maze, which is implied to be a sentient warp in time-space).<br /> <br /> However, there's a literally infinite variety of intruders, some of which aren't truly natives of the Abyss. The Ravaged and the Ludin Sisters from Unbidden spring to mind-yeah, they're jerks, but they're jerks in human ways, and the Ludins are mostly grouchy, apathetic, and petty rather than malicious (and anti-Semites, but they're explicitly not Nazis anymore). They're also humans who have been mutated by the Abyss, and in the case of the Ravaged can be considered victims. I can see a Makara befriending the Ludins and discussing the affairs of the Awakened and reckless over tea, or a Namtaru attempting to find a way for the Ravaged to live without having to flay people.<br /> <br /> I can't say the Begotten would be fans of Abyssal Imprints, though-too much like Heroes, as in almost exactly, except aimed at mages and functioning exactly as they're supposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:13:43-08:00","id":999627,"title":"","content":"I do believe Leliel summed it up best. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only other thing I would add is that most Abyssal Entities are rather short lived. Unless they're one of the more powerful or stable Invaders then I'd imagine they'd be more of a passing fancy for the Begotten. Although if they were one of the more powerful ones...well just image what would happen if a Beast got their hands on the Prince of Fallen Leaves? (Wait, was the Prince of Fallen Leaves an Abyssal Intruder?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 11-07-2016, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:05:45-08:00","id":999641,"title":"","content":"The Prince is an Annunaki, one of several being/worlds that is to Abyssal entities as the Primordial Dream is to Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:32:44-08:00","id":999650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=999641#post999641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prince is an Annunaki, one of several being/worlds that is to Abyssal entities as the Primordial Dream is to Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you think some beasts feel kinship to the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:40:42-08:00","id":999682,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> (characters!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:31:33-08:00","id":999762,"title":"","content":"Can you elaborate on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:45:26-08:00","id":999789,"title":"","content":"Beasts have kinship with posthuman or prehuman monsters - anything like them. As the Beast corebook says, this even leads to a two-tier thing where creatures like werewolves are more Kin than more tangental cases like mages. Demons are sufficiently not-human to not be Kin.<br /> <br /> If an Unchained Demon, a machine-mind pretending to be human, isn't valid for Kinship, then a bundle of poisionous anti-symbols shed from a still born alternate world definitely isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:37:25-08:00","id":999807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=999789#post999789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have kinship with posthuman or prehuman monsters - anything like them. As the Beast corebook says, this even leads to a two-tier thing where creatures like werewolves are more Kin than more tangental cases like mages. Demons are sufficiently not-human to not be Kin.<br /> <br /> If an Unchained Demon, a machine-mind pretending to be human, isn't valid for Kinship, then a bundle of poisionous anti-symbols shed from a still born alternate world definitely isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't Spirits Kin, though? They aren't really post <i>or</i> pre-human.<br /> <br /> And what's not human about Unchained? They eat, sleep, and feel like anyone else. They even have Virtues and Vices. They are, after all, <i>professionally</i> human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:30:46-08:00","id":999881,"title":"","content":"Unchained disguise themselves as humans, and even to an extent identify with humans, but they're not human and never were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:49:52-08:00","id":999927,"title":"","content":"It's kinda irrelevant anyway. However human or not you want Demons to be, the G-M and it's rogue servants still aren't classed as Kin.<br /> <br /> You know, I've always been struck by the parrallel use of the Chaoskampf mythology between the Dark Mother and the Abyss... I could see a Beast being quite intrigued by the similarity up until they actually met something from the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:36:03-08:00","id":1000015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=999789#post999789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have kinship with posthuman or prehuman monsters - anything like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says that creatures which were never human and never will be human (such as &quot;inhuman spirits&quot;) are classed as descended from the night mother and thus they have kinship with. Humanity has nothing to do with whether beasts can consider something kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons are sufficiently not-human to not be Kin. </div> </div> </div>Orange spirits are kin for godsake.... Demons are closer to humans than orange spirits are. It's nothing to do with how human the creature is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If an Unchained Demon, a machine-mind pretending to be human, isn't valid for Kinship </div> </div> </div>Fetches are considered to be descended from the nightmother so being machines infused with supernatural forces who are just pretending to be human has nothing to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-07-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:11:04-08:00","id":1000030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=999789#post999789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts have kinship with posthuman or prehuman monsters - anything like them. As the Beast corebook says, this even leads to a two-tier thing where creatures like werewolves are more Kin than more tangental cases like mages. Demons are sufficiently not-human to not be Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda offtopic but I wanna know, how do Beasts relate to Spirits and Ghosts, if not Angels in that context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:10:49-08:00","id":1000064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000015#post1000015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetches are considered to be descended from the nightmother so being machines infused with supernatural forces who are just pretending to be human has nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but there's an important component of them that's human. The shadow-soul.<br /> <br /> An Unchained is just wearing the face, a fetch is actually a part of their changeling that's been given their own body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T19:00:12-08:00","id":1000083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000064#post1000064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but there's an important component of them that's human. The shadow-soul.<br /> <br /> An Unchained is just wearing the face, a fetch is actually a part of their changeling that's been given their own body.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Unchained is wearing their souls metaphysical position. Pretty sure that's a bit more than the already irrelevant part of a changeling's soul. <br /> <br /> Demons aren't kin because Reasons. Can we move on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:06:58-08:00","id":1000101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000083#post1000083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Unchained is wearing their souls metaphysical position. Pretty sure that's a bit more than the already irrelevant part of a changeling's soul.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't kin because Reasons. Can we move on?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying there's actual reasons, in that the fetch actually literally <i>is </i>a clone of a human, one entirely defined by a posthuman and by their relationship with the life they are replacements for, while for Unchained the identity is a disguise that isn't a fundamental part of their construction like the shadow is (as in, remove it, they get Burned, they don't die),<br /> <br /> Still, I agree that making spirits, of all things, Kin while demons (second-most human splat in the CofD, I've heard them called) is a bit odd. Let's move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:18:32-08:00","id":1000107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000083#post1000083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Unchained is wearing their souls metaphysical position.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's wearing the body and connections that used to be plugged into a proper soul. You can effectively duplicate the parts of this that aren't &quot;you're a shapeshifting fugitive xenocyborg using occult science to accomplish this thing&quot; with liberal applications of brainwashing and plastic surgery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pretty sure that's a bit more than the already irrelevant part of a changeling's soul. </div> </div> </div>The fetch is made by fae magic from an part of or analogue for the human soul torn off on the scourging points of a realm defined by the pain and dreams of humans en route to the abode of one or more godlike fate-monsters. There's ample room for the Begotten to find themselves reflected in the things with a narrative relation to mirrors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons aren't kin because Reasons. </div> </div> </div>Because Themes, if we're to be specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can we move on? </div> </div> </div>Evidently not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:21:54-08:00","id":1000111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000101#post1000101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, I agree that making spirits, of all things, Kin while demons (second-most human splat in the CofD, I've heard them called) is a bit odd. Let's move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes from that aspect of the God-Machine and it's related stuff being sacred, profane, and <i>apart</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:42:45-08:00","id":1000120,"title":"","content":"I also agree it makes perfect sense for Demons to not count as Kin. They are of the God-Machine, not the Dark Mother. I just felt it should be noted that according to the book, the theory of it having to do with &quot;human-ness&quot; is false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T00:33:08-08:00","id":1000175,"title":"","content":"Eh, doesn't matter. No, Abyssal entities aren't kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T00:53:46-08:00","id":1000177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000120#post1000120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree it makes perfect sense for Demons to not count as Kin. They are of the God-Machine, not the Dark Mother. I just felt it should be noted that according to the book, the theory of it having to do with &quot;human-ness&quot; is false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most things aren't of the Dark Mother. Her being the Genesis of most monsters ist just a myth even within the Beast book, a theory Beasts share that isn't really backed up by anything from other books.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000083#post1000083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons aren't kin because Reasons. Can we move on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saw this, a bit late. Sorry, yes, move on. The thread is already gone past the &quot;Demons aren't kin for solely thematic reasons&quot; point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 11-08-2016, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:49:36-08:00","id":1000188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000177#post1000177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most things aren't of the Dark Mother. Her being the Genesis of most monsters ist just a myth even within the Beast book, a theory Beasts share that isn't really backed up by anything from other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best explanation we have so far, but it does seem specifically designed to have a large chance for Beasts to be wrong as to the &quot;why&quot;. But it still obviously isn't because of &quot;human-ness&quot; since... it literally has &quot;inhuman spirits&quot; listed as kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:11:03-08:00","id":1000225,"title":"","content":"If Horrors are created by the nightmares of people, it makes sense that Demons wouldn't have really penetrated the minds and memories of humanity to any large extent. If you make a deal with one, odds are sooner or later your soul is annihilated. If you've just seen one, odds are you've either died doing so or the God-Machine has erased your memories.<br /> <br /> Conversely, spirits and werewolves and witches are routinely intruding on things and affecting mythologies in long-lasting ways.<br /> <br /> There's probably people who know about them, have nightmares about both the Abyss and the Demons, but not to a number comparable with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T09:50:28-08:00","id":1000304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000175#post1000175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, doesn't matter. No, Abyssal entities aren't kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave, I appreciate the position you can speak from as a dev and metaphysics guy, but the existence of a Kinship Nightmare that specifically references the nature of the Abyss, the applicability of Thicker Than Water to feral supernatural beings, and the fact that Family Ties is a Condition that the non-Beast party has to be receptive to all kind of point to the more operative issue with Abyssal Kinship being &quot;good luck getting ahold of a gulmoth or acamoth that's pliable to further tying itself to something that partially defines its ultimately undefinable nature by proxy.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Abyss's thematic relation to destruction and negation is not a valid source of inspiration and relation for the Begotten despite its constituents' being about as driven as any other ephemeral being, that contributes more to the difficulty of readers in academically understanding what the Abyss is about than it does the clarification of how Kinship works in a fashion that is less broad than the Question of Lineage section's &quot;everything but the Unchained&quot; and its implicit macrocategory of &quot;everything not drawn from the God-Machine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can understand not wanting Mage's cosmology getting misunderstood and used inappropriately in the low-level crossover mindset half the fandom seems to operate under by default, as well as the necessity of ensuring that Beasts don't get easy outs for their ties to humanity short of claiming one of the lesser Inheritances, but unless I've missed a substantial chunk of the map here (and I very well could have, between Mage still not being one of the gamelines I have a stronger understanding of and Beast relating to a relatively new element of the cosmology) there's not a readily visible reason for the Children of the Dark Mother to lack even the surface-level shreds of Kinship with beings whose principle ties to the world are the things that they attempt to corrupt and destroy.<br /> <br /> It's highly probable that I'm misunderstanding one or more elements of the games' metaphysics here, but if there's been a miscommunication at some point in the process between writing and reading the book it would be great to get it cleared up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:49:50-08:00","id":1000326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000107#post1000107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's wearing the body and connections that used to be plugged into a proper soul. You can effectively duplicate the parts of this that aren't &quot;you're a shapeshifting fugitive xenocyborg using occult science to accomplish this thing&quot; with liberal applications of brainwashing and plastic surgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brainwashing and plastic surgery can't retroactively change people's genetics, or make them register as completely human. It goes deeper than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000107#post1000107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fetch is made by fae magic from an part of or analogue for the human soul torn off on the scourging points of a realm defined by the pain and dreams of humans en route to the abode of one or more godlike fate-monsters. There's ample room for the Begotten to find themselves reflected in the things with a narrative relation to mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? The human soul doesn't seem remotely important here, and as for the reflection in humanity's fears, the &quot;imposter&quot;-ness of Demons should certainly give some traction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000107#post1000107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Themes, if we're to be specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's out of universe. Inside, there is nothing other than &quot;it just is&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000107#post1000107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evidently not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-08-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:07:00-08:00","id":1000343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000326#post1000326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brainwashing and plastic surgery can retroactively change people's genetics, or make them register as completely human. It goes deeper than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I repeat: The parts that aren't &quot;you're a shapeshifting fugitive xenocyborg using occult science to accomplish this thing.&quot; Having a whole-body donor doesn't make the process any less pseudomundane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So? The human soul doesn't seem remotely important here, </div> </div> </div>&quot;Here&quot; being &quot;a discussion of the ability of a monster that naturally lives in the world within the human soul to relate itself to a supernatural being that requires a part of a human being generally related directly to the soul as opposed to a supernatural being that burns out the soul in a human body to occupy the resulting vacuum.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and as for the reflection in humanity's fears, the &quot;imposter&quot;-ness of Demons should certainly give some traction. </div> </div> </div>The nature of Cover is not the same as the nature of the Mask and the fact that humanity is scared of something about you is not the source of Kinship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but that's out of universe. </div> </div> </div>The Temenos <i>runs on</i> Themes and the Begotten <i>live there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:20:41-08:00","id":1000352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000343#post1000343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I repeat: The parts that aren't &quot;you're a shapeshifting fugitive xenocyborg using occult science to accomplish this thing.&quot; Having a whole-body donor doesn't make the process any less pseudomundane.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000343#post1000343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Here&quot; being &quot;a discussion of the ability of a monster that naturally lives in the world within the human soul to relate itself to a supernatural being that requires a part of a human being generally related directly to the soul as opposed to a supernatural being that burns out the soul in a human body to occupy the resulting vacuum.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Primordial Dream = Temenos? I've seen commentary run either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000343#post1000343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of Cover is not the same as the nature of the Mask and the fact that humanity is scared of something about you is not the source of Kinship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Cover is deeper/more comprehensive than the Mask. The Mask is merely an advanced illusion. And thus far, we haven't really determined what <i>does</i> qualify one for Kinship are than broad, arbitrary categories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000343#post1000343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Temenos <i>runs on</i> Themes and the Begotten <i>live there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are themes <i>as they apply to the game-lines</i>, which do not exist inside said universe. Can you point to where &quot;Unchained and God-Machine Phenomena must be kept apart from other splats to preserve its themes&quot; lives in the Temenos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:37:16-08:00","id":1000362,"title":"","content":"To the Beasts that know about it, the Primordial Dream is Temenos adjacent. But it's a part of the Temenos. They seem to believe that the fears represent a different area entirely, but it's just another part of the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-08-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:37:26-08:00","id":1000363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000352#post1000352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Primordial Dream = Temenos? I've seen commentary run either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's the oldest and deepest chunks of the collective human unconscious, right flush up against the realm of High Speech and by extension Language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thus far, we haven't really determined what <i>does</i> qualify one for Kinship are than broad, arbitrary categories. </div> </div> </div>Hunger, for one thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those are themes <i>as they apply to the game-lines</i>, which do not exist inside said universe. </div> </div> </div>Every place in the Temenos runs on themes to such a degree that those themes <i>serve as symbolic aids for magic</i>. That's pretty well in-universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you point to where &quot;Unchained and God-Machine Phenomena must be kept apart from other splats to preserve its themes&quot; lives in the Temenos? </div> </div> </div>No, because the God-Machine no more lives in the Temenos than vampires do. That doesn't change the fact that the God-Machine works as a collection of discrete deliberate interlocking parts that happens to exploit occult principles rather than as a symbolic net constraining a primal force of consumption, obsession, entropy, etc to a sustainable form of magical phenomena that can direct that supernatural flood-in-waiting.<br /> <br /> Demons don't have frenzy or Obsessions or Torments or any of the other things that innately compel other splats to do the sorts of things that the Begotten have to do or be present for to continue living. They maintain a relatively conscious inventory of their desires and Aether is something they need out of paranoia and pragmatism rather than Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:52:13-08:00","id":1000443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000304#post1000304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Abyss's thematic relation to destruction and negation is not a valid source of inspiration and relation for the Begotten despite its constituents' being about as driven as any other ephemeral being, that contributes more to the difficulty of readers in academically understanding what the Abyss is about than it does the clarification of how Kinship works in a fashion that is less broad than the Question of Lineage section's &quot;everything but the Unchained&quot; and its implicit macrocategory of &quot;everything not drawn from the God-Machine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyss is thematically isn't so much destruction and negation, it's things that aren't a natural part of reality, things that should not be and that are inherently incompatible with the way things are.<br /> If you then have something that is a natural part of our reality come up to an Abyssal and go 'hey, brother, we are connected and you are totally and objectively part of my family, let's hang out and eat some dudes&quot; that kind of defeats the Abyss' most important themes even worse than being kin would destroy Demons'.<br /> At least I'm pretty sure that's why Dave doesn't count Abyssal phenomena as kin.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:18:10-08:00","id":1000455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000443#post1000443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyss is thematically isn't so much destruction and negation, it's things that aren't a natural part of reality, things that should not be and that are inherently incompatible with the way things are.<br /> If you then have something that is a natural part of our reality come up to an Abyssal and go 'hey, brother, we are connected and you are totally and objectively part of my family, let's hang out and eat some dudes&quot; that kind of defeats the Abyss' most important themes even worse than being kin would destroy Demons'.<br /> At least I'm pretty sure that's why Dave doesn't count Abyssal phenomena as kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. The problem is that regardless of how a given Abyssal entity feels about Beasts in general or particular, the primary importance of Kinship is to Beasts themselves and their own perceptions of the world.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be able to completely understand something from the great cosmic womb of unbeing to be able to feel a connection to its destructive aspects and piece together reasons why it is dangerous; people fear and invoke the Abyss regardless of its unpinnable nature. The creatures of the Abyss manifest in ways that fit into the sensory framework of experience regardless of their deeper incomprehensibility, because they manifest in the Phenomenal World \u2014 the Begotten truck in ominous phenomena does not cease to have a point of reference just because there's an ultimate unknowable on the other end of the line.<br /> <br /> Making them not-kin has more consequences than just disqualifying them from the more active Kinship abilities, like rendering a manifested gulmoth as unremarkable to Begotten senses as an unmanifested one. It's a blind spot that doesn't have the same motif of disconnection and compartmentalization and mundanity that the Machine does to justify cutting an entire class of supernatural entity out of an explicitly nigh-universal sense for the immediate presence of supernatural entities. It's one thing to put kinship with &quot;the Abyss&quot; off the table (you might as well try to claim Kinship with &quot;the Wyrd&quot; or &quot;the Shadow&quot;) and another to cut out &quot;any Abyssal entity.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:45:06-08:00","id":1000479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000455#post1000455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The creatures of the Abyss manifest in ways that fit into the sensory framework of experience regardless of their deeper incomprehensibility, because they manifest in the Phenomenal World \u2014 the Begotten truck in ominous phenomena does not cease to have a point of reference just because there's an ultimate unknowable on the other end of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not ultimate unknowables (in fact, sometimes that they are very much knowable is the very essence of why they are dangerous, as with the memetic abyssal math), they are things that don't belong, things that are defined by not being connected to the things of the phenomenal world. The anti-symbols to the truth-symbols of the Supernal.You can't connect them to the world via kinship without making them belong in the world in a way that is counter to their very being. An abyssal intrusion is not just an &quot;ominous phenomena&quot;.<br /> To use a Mage centric explanation (which is the only one that matters, as the Abyss is a Mage specific antagonist) kinship is a supernatural phenomenon that works because the supernal symbols that are the source code of the universe describe it's ability to connect to the it's symbols to those that describe other supernatural. But abyssal phenomena, including those you'd describe as an &quot;Abyssal entity&quot; is anti-symbols spilling into the phenomenal world, and there is no way for the supernal representation of the kinship bond to connect to the abyssal anti symbols of whatever abyssal thing is warping the world next to the Beast in question. An &quot;Abyssal entity&quot; is not a supernatural creature in the common sense, it's anti-symbols that warp reality that happen to take a form that might visually look like a monster, but that is incidental to its nature.<br /> <br /> Again, you can't make Abyssal entities kin without destroying the thematic coherence, and from the PoV of the Mage Line's developer his primary responsibiliy is the the thematic coherence of the things that make up Mage. If that means ruling that Abyssal creatures aren't kin, then that's what he needs to do, because Beasts are of lesser importance than the line he is responsible for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000455#post1000455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a blind spot that doesn't have the same motif of disconnection and compartmentalization and mundanity that the Machine does to justify cutting an entire class of supernatural entity out of an explicitly nigh-universal sense for the immediate presence of supernatural entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something doesn't need to have an identical motif to Demons to have a one that justifies not making them kin.<br /> Abyssal entities have a coherent justification for why they aren't kin, nothing more is required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 11-08-2016, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:33:47-08:00","id":1001091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/998174-abyss-reactions?p=1000479#post1000479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not ultimate unknowables (in fact, sometimes that they are very much knowable is the very essence of why they are dangerous, as with the memetic abyssal math), they are things that don't belong, things that are defined by not being connected to the things of the phenomenal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not defined at all at their roots. That's part of the point. That's what I mean by &quot;ultimate unknowable&quot; \u2014 there is no comprehensible being at the heart of the Annunaki, and that presents no obstacle to their ability to manifest in the Phenomenal World their home serves to occlude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The anti-symbols to the truth-symbols of the Supernal.You can't connect them to the world via kinship without making them belong in the world in a way that is counter to their very being. An abyssal intrusion is not just an &quot;ominous phenomena&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Ominous phenomena \u2014 phenomena that present omens of danger, i.e. warning signs \u2014 are what the fear-response of the Primordial Dream keys off of. It's why Lair Traits are universally negative phenomena that Horrors are immune to by association. Abyssal phenomena enter the world, are usually dangerous, and usually betray that dangerousness through the marks of erosion and corruption evinced by their manifested forms. They don't not-belong in the world enough to be completely barred from entering it in a state that registers to mortal senses and relates to their inner nature, and that is nine tenths of Kinship's practical root basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To use a Mage centric explanation (which is the only one that matters, as the Abyss is a Mage specific antagonist) kinship is a supernatural phenomenon that works because the supernal symbols that are the source code of the universe describe it's ability to connect to the it's symbols to those that describe other supernatural. </div> </div> </div>Kinship connects monsters through sympathy, which is one of the handful of things that Abyssal entities use like any other supernatural being \u2014 it's why the acamoth corrupt dreams and significant or repeated Paradox risks the creation of an Abyssal Verge. Kinship is &quot;these things are alike and their natures align somewhat through that likeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But abyssal phenomena, including those you'd describe as an &quot;Abyssal entity&quot; is anti-symbols spilling into the phenomenal world, and there is no way for the supernal representation of the kinship bond to connect to the abyssal anti symbols of whatever abyssal thing is warping the world next to the Beast in question. </div> </div> </div>It has no problem connecting to the world around it to warp it. The Abyss is everywhere and can blossom forth from pretty much anything, and despite Begotten claims that similarity implies a common root there's not much necessary shared ancestry in Anumerus and the Namtaru who's making nine an unlucky number in their hometown both having &quot;bad-news things tied to numbers&quot; to associate them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An &quot;Abyssal entity&quot; is not a supernatural creature in the common sense, it's anti-symbols that warp reality that happen to take a form that might visually look like a monster, but that is incidental to its nature. </div> </div> </div>The effect Abyssal entities have on the world around them is a consequence of their nature being antithetical to Phenomenal reality in a pure form. They heal and gain Essence from the breakdown of mortal Integrity and their resonance warps their surroundings to become more like the portion of the Abyss that they hail from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that means ruling that Abyssal creatures aren't kin, then that's what he needs to do, because Beasts are of lesser importance than the line he is responsible for. </div> </div> </div>Kinship is literally only important to Beast at all and there are means of establishing that you won't see Beasts forming Family Ties with gulmoth without making an un-creature formed of befouled magic fail to ping the &quot;spot unveiled supernatural creatures&quot; ability without a veil, particularly given that Kinship applies at only two levels and one of them goes away by <i>going away</i>, which is incredibly easy for something whose home de facto cannot exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something doesn't need to have an identical motif to Demons to have a one that justifies not making them kin. </div> </div> </div>When that motif is &quot;the destructively-oriented splat that has most of their powerset work through sympathy and supernatural connections can sometimes detect but not connect with the renegade processes of a sterile and shuttered machine-god-of-no-mythos that offers a wholly-impersonal and task-oriented framework of supernatural power that has to actually assemble its outward spread rather than spilling it everywhere and dealing with the fallout as it comes,&quot; there's not much identical in &quot;the contagious entropy of occult meaning in the universe, which resonates with the failure of supernatural bindings and the corrosion of reality and the primordial beings from the beginning of time and gets many of its connections to the world through those patterns, isn't going to have common cause with a race of befoulers and destroyers and thieves and oath-entrappers spawned from an ever-changing progenitor-beast who is variously identified with figures such as Lilith, Pandora, the titanic Mother of Monsters, and assorted other entities tied intimately to the fear of the unknown and/or unknowable.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}